    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789572422.332391,
      "body": "Here's what I found by checking this environment directly:\n\n- No stored credentials exist anywhere: no `~/.netrc`, no `WANDB_API_KEY` in the environment, and no `wandb` settings directory under `$HOME` or in the repo. `wandb` itself *is* installed correctly in the `surya_ws` env (v0.23.1), so it's not a missing-package issue.\n- The config (`config_script.yaml:212-213`) has `wandb_entity: null`, meaning `WandbLogger` will try to log to your **personal** WandB account, not a team. That's unrelated to login failing, but worth knowing if you were expecting it to land in a shared team project.\n- Outbound reachability to `api.wandb.ai` works from this container, so it's not a network block.\n\nSo the practical conclusion: **nothing has ever logged in successfully on this machine** \u2014 there's simply no credential on disk for `wandb` to use yet.\n\nThe likely reason the interactive flow in the markdown cell isn't working for you: those instructions (\"In VSCode the dialog opens a box at the top of your screen\") describe VS Code's specific handling of `wandb.login()`'s interactive prompt. You're running this in JupyterLab (via the Jupyter MCP tools), where that same prompt shows up differently \u2014 as a plain inline `input()`/API-key text box in the cell output, not a VS Code command-palette dialog. If your JupyterHub setup restricts kernel stdin (common on shared/remote JupyterHub deployments), that `input()` call can hang indefinitely with no error, which looks exactly like \"I can't log in.\"\n\n**What I'd try:** skip the interactive prompt entirely \u2014 get your API key from https://wandb.ai/authorize and set it before creating the logger, either:\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ[\"WANDB_API_KEY\"] = \"your-key-here\"\n```\nor from a terminal (not notebook cell) in this environment:\n```bash\n/home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws/bin/wandb login <your-key>\n```\nThat writes `~/.netrc` directly, bypassing whatever is breaking the interactive dialog.\n\nCan you tell me exactly what happens when you run the `WandbLogger(...)` cell \u2014 does it hang with no output, throw a specific error, or open a prompt that then fails? That'll tell me which of these it actually is rather than me guessing further.",
      "id": "1c0a42d5-ff6e-42ab-a7c7-ff449b2d8061",
      "mentions": [],
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg"
    },
