      "raw_time": false,
      "id": "0fe119fa-e332-4b19-b554-692cd0cd238c",
      "body": "Yes, that worked. `~/.netrc` now exists with a `machine api.wandb.ai` entry and correct `600` permissions \u2014 your API key is stored and `wandb` will pick it up automatically from now on, in any process on this machine (terminal, notebook kernel, training script), without prompting again.\n\n**Next steps in the notebook:**\n\n1. You don't need to restart the kernel \u2014 `WandbLogger` reads `~/.netrc` at the time it authenticates, not at import time, so it'll pick up the key even in a kernel that was already running before you logged in.\n2. Just re-run the `WandbLogger(...)` cell. It should now construct without hanging or prompting.\n3. Then continue to `trainer.fit(lit_model, train_data_loader, val_data_loader)` \u2014 that's the first point a real run gets created and pushed to wandb.ai, so it's the real test. Watch for a line like `wandb: \ud83d\ude80 View run at https://wandb.ai/...` in the output.\n4. Since `wandb_entity: null` in the config, this run logs to your **personal** WandB account under project `template_solar_event_identification` (`config_script.yaml:212`) \u2014 not any shared team project. If you were invited to a team and want the run to land there instead, set `wandb_entity: <team-name>` in the config before running."
    },
