    {
      "body": "I compared your edit against a live check of your WandB credentials, and it's not a typo \u2014 it's a permissions issue.\n\n**Your diff:**\n```diff\n-  wandb_entity: null      # WandB team/org name; null to log to your personal account\n+  wandb_entity: surya-ws2      # WandB team/org name; null to log to your personal account\n```\n\n**What I checked against the live API using the key you just logged in with:**\n- You *are* authenticated (`midhungm2001`), and `surya-ws2` *is* a real team you belong to \u2014 the entity name is spelled correctly.\n- Listing projects under `surya-ws2` works fine: `radioburst_classification`, `simsearch_surya`, `sep_pred_psp`, `flare_detection`, `template_solar_wind_regression`, `template_flare_regression`.\n- But `template_solar_event_identification` \u2014 the project name set in your config (`config_script.yaml:212`) \u2014 **isn't in that list**. It doesn't exist yet under `surya-ws2`.\n\nThat combination \u2014 read access works (you can list/view the team's existing projects), but the write call that creates a new run/project (`upsertBucket`) gets a 403 \u2014 is the classic signature of having a **Viewer** role on that team rather than **Member**/**Admin**. Viewers can browse but can't create new runs or projects; Members can.\n\n**What to do:**\n1. Ask whoever administers the `surya-ws2` team to bump your role there to Member (or Admin). That's the actual fix if you want this run logged under the shared team.\n2. To keep working right now without waiting on that: temporarily set `wandb_entity: null` (log to your personal account) or point `wandb_project` at nothing new and just verify with your admin whether even the existing projects (e.g. `template_flare_regression`) accept writes from your key \u2014 if those also fail, it confirms the role theory rather than the missing-project theory.\n\nWant me to revert `wandb_entity` to `null` in the config so you can keep training and switch to the team entity once your role is upgraded?",
