      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "body": "Good catch \u2014 I was wrong to pin it on your role tier. I re-checked the team directly, and you *are* listed in `surya-ws2`'s member roster, so it's not a missing-membership issue.\n\nWhat I found instead, looking at the team's actual settings via the API:\n\n```\n\"defaultAccess\": \"PRIVATE\",\n\"privateOnly\": true,\n```\n\nThis team enforces private-only projects. Combined with the fact that `template_solar_event_identification` (the project name in your config) doesn't exist yet under `surya-ws2` \u2014 the write that failed was specifically a **create-new-project** call, not a write to an existing one. Many W&B teams restrict who can create *new* projects to admins, separately from general Member/Viewer role \u2014 being a Member doesn't automatically mean you can create projects, only that you can write to ones that already exist and you have access to.\n\nThat's consistent with everything we've seen: you can list/read the team's existing projects fine, but the specific call that failed (`upsertBucket`, which both creates a run *and* the project if it's new) got rejected with the same \"cannot access this resource\" message a project-creation restriction would produce.\n\n**To confirm this without guessing further**, the cleanest test is to point your run at a project that already exists in that team \u2014 e.g. `template_flare_regression` \u2014 instead of the new name. If a run logs successfully there, it confirms the problem is project-creation permission, not team access in general.\n\nWant me to update `wandb_project` in the config to `template_flare_regression` temporarily so you can test that? (I'd rather have you confirm before I create a run in a shared team project, since other people on that team would see it appear.) Alternatively, you could ask whoever administers `surya-ws2` (I see Andr\u00e9s Mu\u00f1oz-Jaramillo in the member list) to either create the `template_solar_event_identification` project for you or confirm the team's project-creation policy.",
